<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nectanebo I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 362 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> · Also known as Nakhtnebef</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nectanebo I was the founder of the Thirtieth Dynasty, the last native dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, reigning from 380 to 362 BCE. A general from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sebennytos">Sebennytos</a> in the Delta, he deposed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepherites-ii">Nepherites II</a> of the Twenty-ninth Dynasty. In 373 BCE he repelled a Persian invasion led by Pharnabazus and the Athenian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iphicrates">Iphicrates</a>, helped by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> flood, and he was a great temple builder, with works at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philae">Philae</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnak">Karnak</a> and elsewhere.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nectanebo-i.jpg" alt="Nectanebo I" width="320" height="367" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marco Prins · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nectanebo_I_with_khepresh_crown.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
